    summary_en: "The European Commission will allocate €36 million through the Digital Europe Programme (DEP) to support the establishment of the 'EU Cybersecurity Reserve.' This mechanism aims to enhance the cyber resilience of the EU, its member states, and third countries related to the DEP. The reserve will include incident response services from trusted service providers, designed to address and recover from large-scale cyber incidents affecting EU member states, EU institutions, and critical and highly critical sectors (such as healthcare or energy). ENISA will use these funds over three years to procure and manage these incident response services through public tenders and service demand assessments. This move strengthens the EU's coordinated response capability during cyber incidents, particularly for critical infrastructure covered by the NIS2 Directive.",
